From ed9289f77bbc6c3e708c194f0ccdea260d79a26c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HiGarfield <HiGarfield@126.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:45:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build: support OpenSSL 1.0.2 and GCC 7.5

Add a single OpenSSL compatibility header and pin the C standard so the
daemon builds on older targets (GCC 7.5, OpenSSL 1.0.2).

- openssl_compat.h: derive macros from OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER; provide
  aliases (dns_unconst, dns_TLS_*_method, dns_SSL_write, ...).
- Fix -Wdiscarded-qualifiers on OpenSSL 1.0/1.1: drop const only below 3.0.
- Replace OPENSSL_API_COMPAT guards with SMARTDNS_NEED_LEGACY_INIT;
  no-op thread setup on 1.1.0+.
- Pin -std=gnu11; fix feature probes (void main -> int main(void)).

Verified against OpenSSL 1.0.2u/1.1.1w/3.0.13 and gcc-11..16 + clang-17/18.
